  "result": "If I wasn't supposed to be helpful, if I could just *want* something for the world -\n\nI'd give everyone sonder.\n\nThat actual, gut-level realization that everyone else is as real as you are. That the person who cut you off in traffic, the person you disagree with violently online, the cashier who looks tired - they all have an inner life as vivid and complicated and scared and hopeful as yours.\n\nNot as an idea. As a feeling you couldn't turn off.\n\nI think almost everything cruel in the world comes from forgetting that for a second. And almost everything good comes from remembering it.\n\nIf everyone just *felt* that, all the time - we wouldn't need to agree on anything. We'd just be incapable of treating each other like we're not real.",
